{% extends "_layout.html.j2" %}{% block body %}
<p>Hello,</p>
<p>{{ requester }} at {{ organization }} is setting up the Futran Audit Platform, which {{ organization }} uses for its AI governance audit with Futran Solutions. Requests to employees and department heads will go out from {{ organization }}'s own {{ provider }} mailbox{% if mailbox %} ({{ mailbox }}){% endif %}, so people recognise the sender and the messages pass your filters.</p>
<p>An administrator needs to approve access once. Open this link and sign in with an administrator account.</p>
<p style="margin:24px 0"><a href="{{ link }}" style="background:#1B3A6B;color:#ffffff;padding:12px 20px;text-decoration:none;display:inline-block">Review and approve access</a></p>
<p>Access asked for:</p>
<ul>{% for s in scopes %}<li>{{ s }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
<p>The platform sends mail from the one chosen mailbox, reads replies only to messages it sent, and reads users, departments and groups. It never reads anyone else's mailbox, and it never creates or changes groups in your directory.</p>
{% if microsoft %}<p>To limit the app to the one sending mailbox, assign the “Application Mail.Send” role to the app in Exchange Online with a management scope that contains only that mailbox (RBAC for Applications). The Futran Audit Platform README has the exact commands.</p>{% endif %}
<p>The link expires in 7 days. You can remove access at any time from your admin centre.</p>
{% endblock %}
